    escalation: 'Agregación que sigue en error tras credencial, schema y correlación: caso con el soporte de SailPoint adjuntando los errores textuales de la corrida y el id de la fuente. Agente/cluster de la fuente caído (la virtual appliance del conector): dueño de la infraestructura y líder de IAM — sin agente no hay agregación que reparar. Fuentes del negocio (no AD) con datos de RRHH inconsistentes: dueño de RRHH del sistema — el IAM repara el conector, no los datos de origen.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, the IdentityNow connector issue reported under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} has been diagnosed and corrected. The aggregation was failing due to an expired connector credential combined with an outdated source schema; we updated the connector credentials with the current service account, refreshed the schema, and ran a full aggregation of the source with zero errors. We validated the complete cycle with a test account: new and changed identities now flow from the source of truth into the platform, and provisioning back to the directory works. The connector is back on its normal schedule and its last run is green.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'SailPoint IdentityNow source desynchronization remediated at {{TIMESTAMP}}: sources enumerated via /v3/sources to identify the affected connector, Test Connection isolated the failing layer (invalid credentials after a service account rotation that missed this consumer), credentials refreshed and the directory service account validated (Enabled, not locked, coherent PasswordLastSet). Full aggregation executed with per-run counters (created/updated/unchanged) and error text captured; account correlation validated against the identity profile attributes (EmployeeID/sAMAccountName), source schema refreshed for new attributes and entitlements, and the provisioning cycle tested end to end with a test account including write permission verification on the target OU. Source left on schedule with a green last-run status.',
